  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "tnilwIdz7c0GFyYOxtauzFILOT4=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:18.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`getReadModel<T>(name: string): T` is the processor's read path into materialized views the reactor already maintains. It is a name lookup with a cast, and it **throws** when the name is not registered \u2014 there is no undefined return to check.\n\nThe reactor ships four built-ins:\n\n| Name | Type | What it gives you |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `\"document-view\"` | `IDocumentView` | Document snapshots for reads: `get()`, `find()`, consistency tracking |\n| `\"document-indexer\"` | `IDocumentIndexer` | Parent/child document relationships and metadata |\n| `\"processor-manager\"` | `IProcessorManager` | Routes operations to registered processors |\n| `\"subscription-notification\"` | `SubscriptionNotificationReadModel` | Notifies subscription callbacks on document change |\n\nCustom read models registered through `IReadModelCoordinator` resolve by their `name` property the same way.\n\nThe throwing behaviour drives where you call it. Resolve read models in the **factory**, not inside `onOperations`, so a missing dependency fails loudly at registration rather than on the first operation batch:\n\n```typescript\nexport const budgetCheckProcessorFactory =\n  (module: IProcessorHostModule) =>\n  async (driveHeader: PHDocumentHeader): Promise<ProcessorRecord[]> => {\n    const budgetModel = module.getReadModel<IBudgetReadModel>(\"budget\");\n    const processor = new BudgetCheckProcessor(module.dispatch, budgetModel);\n    return [{ processor, filter: { branch: [\"main\"], documentId: [\"*\"],\n      documentType: [\"powerhouse/expense-report\"], scope: [\"global\"] } }];\n  };\n```\n\nIf the read model is genuinely optional, wrap the factory call in try/catch and degrade \u2014 the docs call this out explicitly. Note also that in Connect the read models available to `getReadModel` are exactly `reactorModule.readModelCoordinator.readModels`, which is only populated on the in-process reactor path.\n\nProvenance: academy `03-Build/04-WorkWithData/05-ProcessorBestPractices.md` (published), wiring confirmed in `apps/connect/src/store/processor-host-module.ts` at 6.2.2-dev.45.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:18.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:18.000Z"
    }
  },
